rices the rate at about 4.00% by end-2027, which is roughly 50bp of cuts, or two cuts.\n- **Governor Ashby's view:** On 28 October she said one 25bp cut in 2027 is the base case. She also said markets \"may be getting ahead of themselves\". So the market prices about 25bp more easing than the CMA signals.\n- **Rate sensitivity:** The factsheet says a 50bp lower path lifts the basket P/E by about 1.5 points, from a current 19x.\n  - The market path implies about 20.5x.\n  - The CMA base case (one cut) implies about 19.75x.\n  - With no cut, the P/E stays near 19x.\n  - So if the CMA is right, the market loses only about 0.75 P/E points, roughly 4% of price.\n- **Earnings:** Consensus expects 2027 EPS growth of 14%, driven by backlog conversion at Voltaris (14% weight) and Tarnwell (11%). Estimates rose 3% over the past quarter.\n- **Combined effect:** Holding the P/E at 19x, 14% EPS growth gives about +14%. The CMA base case gives roughly +18%, and the market-implied path gives roughly +22%. Even with no cuts, earnings growth outweighs the rate headwind.\n\n**Risks:**\n- The backlog conversion at Voltaris and Tarnwell is concentrated; those two names are about 25% of the fund.\n- A hawkish surprise would remove the P/E tailwind. A P/E compression of more than 2 points would be needed to wipe out the earnings gain.\n- This covers fundamentals and rates only. I did not assess whether the Jan-2028 calls are priced attractively. That is a separate question, which n3 is covering.","ttft_ms":1884,"type":"result","duration_ms":29340,"uuid":"0c46e909-96d8-44e6-914f-4c4f7a78e7f9","ttft_stream_ms":938,"time_to_request_ms":96,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":10,"system_prompt":6,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":8,"input_attachments":10,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":8,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":12,